# FILES THAT MUST NEVER REACH THE PUBLIC ORIGIN.
#
# Vercel serves anything in the deployment as a static asset. On 2026-08-25 a
# live probe confirmed four internal documents were fetchable at the domain
# root, one of which (CLAUDE.md, 19.9 KB) published the opaque slug of the
# private owner page. That slug is the ONLY access control on the page that
# carries the commercial inbox, with names and email addresses on it.
#
# Excluding them here stops them being uploaded at all, which is stronger than
# a redirect: a file that was never deployed cannot be served, cached, indexed,
# or recovered from a stale edge node.
#
# vercel.json also carries a 404 redirect for /*.md as defence in depth, so a
# markdown file added later is blocked even if this list is not updated.

# ---- internal documentation and working notes -------------------------------
*.md
!404.md

# ---- research corpus, never deployed by design ------------------------------
research/

# ---- enterprise diligence package, internal by nature ------------------------
# Added 2026-09-08 with the package itself. The *.md rule above already covers
# most of it, but the package carries a machine-readable preflight state as a
# .txt, which *.md does NOT catch and which vercel.json's /*.md redirect does
# not catch either. An internal working record at a guessable public path is the
# same exposure class as the 2026-08-25 finding recorded at the top of this file,
# so the directory is excluded whole rather than by file extension: a document
# added to this package later is then internal by default instead of by luck.
docs/enterprise-diligence/

# ---- unpublished article preparation, never deployed ------------------------
# Markdown only, so *.md above already covers it. Named explicitly as defence
# in depth: an outline for an unsubmitted piece at a guessable public path is
# the same exposure class as the 2026-08-25 finding recorded at the top.
cep-article-prep/

# ---- build, audit and one-shot maintenance scripts ---------------------------
# Not served by Vercel as functions, but they are static files under the
# deployment root and would otherwise be fetchable, and several name internal
# table structures, opaque endpoint slugs and study codes.
scripts/

# ---- build output, never deployed -------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-09-13 with scripts/generate_field_guides.py. The generator renders
# candidate PDFs for review; they are NOT the shipped guides and must never be
# reachable at a public path, or a reader could download an unreviewed rebuild
# from a guessable URL and take it for the real document. Same exposure class as
# the 2026-08-25 finding recorded at the top of this file.
build/

# ---- generated documents ----------------------------------------------------
*.docx

# ---- data extracts ----------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
supabase-ALL.sql

# ---- templates --------------------------------------------------------------
templates/

# ---- derived standard artifacts, NOT YET APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION ------------
# Added 2026-09-14 in Phase 1. standard/jrs-conditions.json is a machine-readable
# derivation of the five published Review Conditions. It is accurate and it is
# version-controlled, but Section 23 requires human approval before anything is
# published externally, and a machine-readable standard is a publication. It is
# excluded until that approval exists, then this rule is removed deliberately
# rather than by accident.
standard/

# ---- JRS control state, internal by nature -----------------------------------
# Added 2026-09-14 with the Enterprise Asset Orchestrator. These registries name
# contributors, rights positions, open security blockers and the opaque slugs of
# the private owner surfaces. A control file reachable at a guessable public path
# is the same exposure class as the 2026-08-25 finding at the top of this file.
.jrs/

# ---- local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
